ISO-10303-21;
/* Twi092: CLOSED_SHELL with two ADVANCED_FACEs: face0 on CONICAL_SURFACE (half-angle 5°, height 10.0, apex at origin); outer EDGE_LOOP contains only THREE edges — lat_L(v_apex_s→v_base_0), base_arc(v_base_0→v_base_pi), lat_R(v_base_pi→v_apex_e); v_apex_s and v_apex_e are two distinct VERTEX_POINTs both at (0,0,0); the degenerate apex-bridge edge connecting v_apex_s↔v_apex_e was DROPPED silently by the exporter — re-imported wire is incomplete; cone is very pointed (5° half-angle, height 10) → extreme sliver aspect; face1 is a base disk circle face that closes the shell and pushes vertex count; all edges ARE wired into EDGE_LOOPs → FACE_OUTER_BOUNDs → ADVANCED_FACEs in CLOSED_SHELL — never orphaned */
